# Supabase connection strings — TEMPLATE, no values.
#
# These are not set "on Supabase". Supabase yields them; they are then set on
# Vercel (web) and Railway (worker, ws-gateway). Substitute <project-ref>,
# <region> and the role passwords from the project's own connection settings.
#
# Reference: deploy/ENVIRONMENT.md · Cutover order: deploy/MIGRATE-HOSTING.md
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Three roles, three privileges. Never collapse them into one URL.
#   wezesha_app      RLS ENFORCED   — every request path
#   wezesha_service  BYPASSRLS      — system paths only (alerts, auth, audit)
#   postgres         owner          — migrations only, never a runtime host
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Vercel (web) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Serverless: many short-lived instances, each running one query at a time.
# connection_limit=1 is correct HERE and wrong on the worker.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wezesha_app.<project-ref>:<app-role-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1
SERVICE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wezesha_service.<project-ref>:<service-role-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1

# --- Railway (worker, ws-gateway) -------------------------------------------
# One long-lived process running several queues at once. Same host, role and
# password as above; only the pool settings differ. Copying the serverless
# connection_limit here is what starved the nightly forecast twice.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wezesha_app.<project-ref>:<app-role-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=10&pool_timeout=20
# SERVICE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://wezesha_service.<project-ref>:<service-role-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=10&pool_timeout=20

# --- Migrations only --------------------------------------------------------
# Direct, unpooled, owner role. Belongs on the ops machine or CI — never on a
# runtime host. pg_dump also needs this one: transaction pooling breaks it,
# with an error that looks like a permissions problem and is not.
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://postgres:<owner-password>@db.<project-ref>.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pooled means port 6543 in transaction mode, and pgbouncer=true disables
# Prisma's prepared statements because transaction pooling breaks them. The
# tenant client sets app.tenant_id transaction-locally in the same transaction
# as each query, so nothing leaks across recycled connections.
#
# After restoring into a new project, the two roles do not exist yet and the
# grants do not survive a --no-privileges dump. Create both and re-grant before
# expecting any of these URLs to work: deploy/MIGRATE-HOSTING.md, steps 3-4.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
